course: dictionary
lesson: 10418
title: Triple: three times as much
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Triple means three times as much or as many. If you triple 5, you get 15. In a sentence, «Most babies roughly triple their birth weight in their first year» tells you that a baby's weight becomes about three times bigger in that first year.
explain: Triple can also mean having three parts or happening three times, like a triple jump, which is hop, step and jump. Look for clue words around it, such as numbers, "times" or "parts", to help you work out which meaning is right.
explain: Triple can be a verb too. To triple something is to make it three times bigger. Triples, tripled and tripling are its other forms. Check any meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «most babies roughly become three times heavier» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Triple means three times as much or as many.
fact: To triple a number means to multiply it by 3, so tripling 5 gives 15.
fact: Triple can mean having three parts, as in a triple-decker sandwich.
fact: In sport, the triple jump is hop, step and jump.
fact: A triple scoop ice cream has three scoops.
exercise: «Most babies roughly triple their birth weight in their first year.» What does triple mean here? | Three days old | *Three times as much | Half as much | Very quickly
exercise: Tripling 5 gives what? | *15 | 8 | 10 | 53
exercise: In sport, what are the three parts of a triple jump? | Run, run, run | *Hop, step and jump | Kick, catch and throw | Swim, cycle and run
test: «Her triple scoop ice cream had three scoops.» What does triple mean in this sentence? | Made of paper | Very cold | Half full | *Having three parts
test: Which verb means to make something three times bigger? | To rhyme | *To triple | To whisper | To halve
exam: Ella says triple means three times as much, so tripling 4 gives what? | *12 | 7 | 34 | 4
